<p>Use the following procedure to register classification code and user 
 code.</p>
<h2>Registering a Classification Code</h2>
<p>If you register classification codes, the printer logs the number of 
 prints made under each code. </p>
<p>You can register classification codes to individual users and purposes, 
 enabling you to monitor printer usage by each.</p>
<p>For example, you can manage accounts according to individual clients 
 or account titles.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Depending on the classification code setting specified 
 on the printer, jobs without a classification code might be canceled. 
 For details, see the operating instructions provided with the printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Setup</span> 
 menu of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Classification Code:</span> 
 box, enter a classification code using up to 32 characters (a-z, A-Z, 
 0-9, "_", "-").</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2>Registering User Code</h2>
<p>When user codes are registered, the number of prints made under each 
 user code is recorded in the printer. Setting a user code, for example, 
 for each department or individual enables you to track their printer usage.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>When the user authentication function is used, 
 user code setting becomes invalid.</p></li>
<li><p>If a user code is set in an external application 
 (such as utility software), you cannot set a user code in this driver.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Setup</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">User Code:</span> 
 box, enter a user code using up to eight digits.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
